- op: update  # 2c65
  at: '2026-09-21T08:49:12Z'  # 2c65
  by: agent  # 2c65
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2c65
  clock: 9  # 2c65
  nonce: 2c65  # 2c65
  set:  # 2c65
    description: "Phase 4 of the ADR-0006 Return-Type Registry Pre-Pass. Promote py.py's local return-type extraction -- `_declared_return_type_name` (py.py:373), consumed by the var_types fill loop at py.py:5900 -- to a global registry entry so untyped Python code can chain through annotated APIs.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n(1) New 'signatures' YAML in python.yaml. PEP 484 annotations are well-defined; map function_definition node types to the existing return_type extraction logic.\n\n(2) Tier 2 escape hatches in signatures.py python_extract(): handle Optional[T], Union[T, U], Awaitable[T], and the 3.9+ T | None pipe syntax. Resolve forward references / string annotations only when trivially decodable.\n\n(3) Wire registry into py.py's var_types fill loop (py.py:5900). The existing local read stays in place: `_declared_return_type_name` (py.py:373) reads the fact from its declared home `Symbol.meta[\"return_type\"]`, which py.py stamps in Pass 1 at py.py:3168 (methods) and py.py:3284 (functions). The new code path just adds a global lookup that fires when the local one would otherwise return None.\n\n(4) Untyped Python remains 'n/a' (registry entry simply absent for unannotated functions).\n\n(5) Regression tests in tests/test_python_signature_registry.py covering: simple return type, Optional unwrap, Union, async Awaitable, string forward reference, untyped function (registry-miss path).\n\n(6) Bakeoff validation: kserve (mixed-typed Python — its public API uses PEP 484 throughout).\n\nPREREQUISITE: Phase 3 (created above) — registry plumbing. Phase 4 ships independently as long as Phases 1-3 have established the registry contract."  # 2c65
- op: discuss  # 9ae2
  at: '2026-09-21T08:49:12Z'  # 9ae2
  by: agent  # 9ae2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9ae2
  clock: 10  # 9ae2
  nonce: 9ae2  # 9ae2
  message: "REFERENCE CORRECTED -- and the citation was never right in the first place.\n\n`py.py:1648` appeared twice in this row's description and now points at the live sites. But the check that matters came back badly: at the commit immediately BEFORE this row was created (b1a61e3b7f, 2026-04-07T18:30-04:00), py.py:1648 sat inside `_extract_inheritance_edges` -- class inheritance, not return types. The local return-type extraction was at py.py:152 (`_extract_return_type_name`), and its var_types consumer at py.py:2167. So this was a WRONG CITATION ON THE DAY IT WAS FILED, not a line number that drifted afterwards. Recording that explicitly, because \"the line moved\" and \"the line was never there\" warrant different amounts of trust in the rest of the row.\n\nWHAT THE ROW POINTS AT NOW, and what moved under it:\n\n  - `_extract_return_type_name` is GONE. WI-ribak (#1117, c9652b836e) deleted it. It parsed the return type back OUT of `Symbol.signature`; ADR-0058 ruled that every fact inside a signature string is read from its declared home and never re-parsed from the display string.\n  - Python's home for the fact is now `Symbol.meta[\"return_type\"]`, stamped in Pass 1 at py.py:3168 (methods) and py.py:3284 (functions).\n  - The reader is `_declared_return_type_name` (py.py:373); the var_types fill loop consumes it at py.py:5900.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR DELIVERABLE (3) -- same shape, different substance. \"The existing local extraction stays in place\" now means a declared-home READ stays in place. A registry lookup would fire where that read returns None, i.e. where the callee's own analyzer never stamped `return_type` -- the cross-file / cross-repo case this row is actually about. Still unbuilt.\n\nPARTIAL OVERLAP WITH DELIVERABLE (2). \"Resolve forward references / string annotations only when trivially decodable\" is shipped for the LOCAL reader: #1118 (0c611ba000) unquotes a quoted forward reference in `_declared_return_type_name` when the inner text is an identifier. A quoted GENERIC is still not decoded, and that was measured to change nothing on this corpus. The registry side of (2) -- Optional[T], Union, Awaitable, the 3.9+ pipe -- is untouched.\n\nNOT RE-SCOPED. Status, priority, and deliverables (1), (4), (5), (6) are unchanged; this is a citation fix plus the premise drift I found while making it. Phase 3 remains the stated prerequisite."  # 9ae2
